 relation to sets from mei altogether; set {lo se mei} to be zi'o in all ca=
ses and leave it at that. The better solution would be to figure out, in a =
formal sense, what exactly about "a can of oranges" causes it to make sense=
 to say "half of a can of oranges", and more importantly what makes "a half=
 a person" make only figurative (or, I suppose, cannibalistic, if you're in=
to that sort of thing) sense.
